WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.677 --> 00:00:02.269
We got Dr. Isaacson.

2
00:00:03.781 --> 00:00:07.080
All right. You guys go check it out.
I'm expected at the office.

3
00:00:07.284 --> 00:00:08.273
Hubb?

4
00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:11.613
Get ready for the smackdown.
He's gonna come at you hard.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.074
-== [ www.OpenSubtitles.org ] ==-

6
00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:57.861
- Who is it?
- N.Y.P.D.

7
00:01:00.671 --> 00:01:02.263
- Dr. Isaacson?
- Yeah.

8
00:01:02.472 --> 00:01:05.566
Detective Ornelas. N.Y.P.D.
This is my partner. Detective Ward.

9
00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:08.006
- We'd like to ask a couple questions.
- Why?

10
00:01:08.378 --> 00:01:09.936
What do you want?
Why are you here?

11
00:01:10.147 --> 00:01:13.776
Calm down. We just wanna ask you
a few questions about a patient.

12
00:01:13.984 --> 00:01:16.578
Patient? What patient?
Come on. you know what time it is?

13
00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:20.419
Listen. I'm sorry. I must go.
I really didn't do anything.

14
00:01:20.624 --> 00:01:22.990
- I'm sorry. Good night.
- Doctor. if we could...

15
00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:28.890
Douche bag's pinned out of his mind.
He thinks we're here to bust him.

16
00:01:31.401 --> 00:01:33.198
Dr. Isaacson. please.

17
00:01:33.403 --> 00:01:36.668
We have reason to believe your life
is in danger. grave danger.

18
00:01:37.741 --> 00:01:40.608
We think one of your patients
is trying to kill you.

19
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:46.872
Kill me?

20
00:01:47.084 --> 00:01:50.451
I'm Agent Salinger with Interpol.
We're assisting in this manhunt.

21
00:01:50.654 --> 00:01:54.055
Why would a patient wanna kill me?
I'm an orthopedist.

22
00:01:54.258 --> 00:01:57.557
This man's a psychotic. He's already
butchered seven doctors in Europe.

23
00:01:57.761 --> 00:02:00.594
We got some serious evidence
to suggest you may be next.

24
00:02:00.797 --> 00:02:02.094
Have you ever seen this man?

25
00:02:04.468 --> 00:02:07.232
No. no. I don't think so.

26
00:02:07.437 --> 00:02:10.998
Does the name Timothy Sherwood
mean anything to you. doctor?

27
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.938
No. How do you know
he's a patient of mine?

28
00:02:14.144 --> 00:02:15.202
We have his footprint.

29
00:02:15.412 --> 00:02:17.937
Yeah. the shoe was manufactured
by AGM Biomechanics...

30
00:02:18.148 --> 00:02:22.482
...exclusively for the Isaacson Institute.
model K-A-F-O 1-2-1.

31
00:02:22.686 --> 00:02:24.449
K-A-F-O 1-2-1?

32
00:02:24.655 --> 00:02:26.748
We started prescribing
that three years ago.

33
00:02:27.124 --> 00:02:28.989
We've used it on hundreds
of our patients.

34
00:02:29.192 --> 00:02:32.252
Well. then we're gonna need
to review all of your files.

35
00:02:32.863 --> 00:02:33.955
Right now?

36
00:02:34.164 --> 00:02:38.191
Doctor. we need to find this man
before he finds you.

37
00:02:39.836 --> 00:02:43.465
- What are you trying to do here. Ella?
- I'm doing my job.

38
00:02:43.674 --> 00:02:46.268
You have any idea of the shitstorm
you've gotten me into?

39
00:02:46.476 --> 00:02:49.070
- We're just trying to get to the truth.
- I get it.

40
00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:53.581
You need to remember there's what
people wanna hear. wanna believe...

41
00:02:53.784 --> 00:02:56.218
...there's everything else.
then there's the truth.

42
00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.719
And since when is that okay?
I can't believe you're saying this to me.

43
00:02:59.923 --> 00:03:01.982
The truth means responsibility. Arnie.

44
00:03:02.192 --> 00:03:05.161
Exactly. which is why
everyone dreads it.

45
00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.894
Look...

46
00:03:15.872 --> 00:03:20.571
The IBBC is using one assassin
for all their hits...

47
00:03:21.011 --> 00:03:23.809
...and we've tracked him here
to New York.

48
00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:28.111
This guy can bury them.

49
00:03:31.154 --> 00:03:34.317
They want me to put a gun
to your head.

50
00:03:34.758 --> 00:03:37.522
You don't find this guy.
and I mean quick...

51
00:03:37.728 --> 00:03:39.958
...they're gonna make me
pull the trigger.

52
00:03:45.235 --> 00:03:47.169
- Do you want dessert?
- No. thank you.

53
00:03:47.704 --> 00:03:49.331
I'd like one.

54
00:03:49.673 --> 00:03:52.267
This is a game that rewards
patience and balance.

55
00:03:52.476 --> 00:03:55.968
You must think like a man of action
and act like a man of thought.

56
00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:09.186
Gentlemen.

57
00:04:09.393 --> 00:04:12.157
<i>Sorry to disturb you at home.</i>
<i>I'm afraid this couldn't wait.</i>

58
00:04:12.929 --> 00:04:14.157
Yes?

59
00:04:14.364 --> 00:04:16.559
<i>Salinger was in Milan.</i>

60
00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.291
<i>Whitman too.</i>

61
00:04:18.502 --> 00:04:19.764
<i>They have the scent.</i>

62
00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.838
<i>It's only a matter of time</i>
<i>before they find our consultant.</i>

63
00:04:30.914 --> 00:04:32.438
Any recommendations?

64
00:04:32.649 --> 00:04:34.674
<i>I strongly advise</i>
<i>against doing anything...</i>

65
00:04:34.885 --> 00:04:37.251
<i>... that would heighten your exposure</i>
<i>right now.</i>

66
00:04:37.454 --> 00:04:39.786
<i>Wilhelm. we've leveraged ourselves</i>
<i>over the edge.</i>

67
00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.925
<i>If we don't meet the delivery date.</i>
<i>buyers will cancel orders...</i>

68
00:04:43.126 --> 00:04:44.457
<i>... our plans will implode...</i>

69
00:04:44.661 --> 00:04:47.027
<i>... and this bank will be left</i>
<i>a bill it cannot pay.</i>

70
00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.460
<i>Heightening exposure</i>
<i>is the least of our problems.</i>

71
00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:51.930
<i>I agree.</i>
<i>We're about to engage Calvini's sons.</i>

72
00:04:52.135 --> 00:04:54.296
<i>We can't allow anyone</i>
<i>to put our agenda at risk.</i>

73
00:04:54.504 --> 00:04:56.802
<i>We must sever all ties</i>
<i>with the consultant.</i>

74
00:04:57.007 --> 00:04:59.168
<i>Consider the mark. gentlemen.</i>

75
00:04:59.376 --> 00:05:04.313
<i>Doing this could be</i>
<i>a very messy affair.</i>

76
00:05:04.514 --> 00:05:06.744
<i>Well. then make it one.</i>

77
00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.544
<i>I don't know why you pay me</i>
<i>to advise on these matters.</i>

78
00:05:09.753 --> 00:05:13.621
<i>It is clear that you don't want my</i>
<i>counsel. only my corroboration.</i>

79
00:05:13.824 --> 00:05:17.419
<i>Really. Wilhelm. We've had</i>
<i>just about all we can take of you.</i>

80
00:05:17.627 --> 00:05:22.587
<i>Yes. I've had about all I can take</i>
<i>of myself.</i>

81
00:05:23.533 --> 00:05:25.831
<i>How would you like us to proceed?</i>

82
00:05:30.607 --> 00:05:34.338
Cassian. what does one do when
there's no way out of a situation?

83
00:05:34.744 --> 00:05:36.609
If there's no way out...

84
00:05:37.814 --> 00:05:41.181
...the best thing is
to find a way further in.

85
00:06:01.104 --> 00:06:03.868
- Fucking disgusting. you know that?
- What are you. my mother?

86
00:06:04.074 --> 00:06:06.975
No. but I could be your old man
for all you know. asshole.

87
00:06:18.088 --> 00:06:19.646
Hey. doc.

88
00:06:22.058 --> 00:06:23.457
Gabriel Hansen?

89
00:06:24.194 --> 00:06:27.755
I don't know.
My associate handled this.

90
00:06:28.665 --> 00:06:31.395
Well. the address
is a post-office box...

91
00:06:32.269 --> 00:06:34.794
...and he paid cash
for all of his medical bills.

92
00:06:36.239 --> 00:06:39.868
There are no diagnostic photos.
Why?

93
00:06:41.878 --> 00:06:43.641
- I don't know.
- Is there a number?

94
00:06:43.847 --> 00:06:49.615
Yeah. 212-157-6421.

95
00:06:55.492 --> 00:06:56.481
It's a dead line.

96
00:07:02.666 --> 00:07:04.896
I'll put a call in to Hubby.
have her run it down.

97
00:07:05.101 --> 00:07:07.899
See if we can't get a crack warrant
for the P.O. Box in Jersey.

98
00:07:12.509 --> 00:07:16.001
What do all these GT's
next to the appointment entries mean?

99
00:07:16.646 --> 00:07:19.274
We have a kickback account
with Go Taxi...

100
00:07:19.783 --> 00:07:22.547
...and they indicate when we
use their service for a patient.

101
00:07:25.355 --> 00:07:27.050
<i>Hey. Hubb says you caught a lead.</i>

102
00:07:27.257 --> 00:07:29.191
Yeah. we've got an address.
We're en route.

103
00:07:29.392 --> 00:07:30.984
- <i>What is it?</i>
- Well. it could be him.

104
00:07:31.194 --> 00:07:32.422
- <i>Really?</i>
- Yeah.

105
00:07:32.629 --> 00:07:35.462
<i>Well. they gotta bring him in now.</i>
<i>This is our last shot.</i>

106
00:07:35.665 --> 00:07:37.223
What do you mean. "our last shot"?

107
00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:40.301
<i>Arnie and I had it out last night.</i>
<i>and our clock's run out.</i>

108
00:07:40.837 --> 00:07:44.568
<i>If we don't get this guy right now.</i>
<i>it's over.</i>

109
00:07:46.376 --> 00:07:48.640
Well. it better be him. then.

110
00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.922
I'm here. Yeah.

111
00:08:06.263 --> 00:08:07.252
I know that.

112
00:08:07.464 --> 00:08:09.261
This is definitely the right address?

113
00:08:09.466 --> 00:08:13.459
Checked the log myself. This is where
they dropped him off every time.

114
00:08:14.704 --> 00:08:16.695
Well. he could be anywhere.

115
00:08:19.643 --> 00:08:22.305
- What do you think he was doing?
- Beats the shit out of me.

116
00:08:22.512 --> 00:08:23.570
It's a big. empty lot.

117
00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.647
Well. I'm starving. I'm gonna
get something. You want anything?

118
00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:27.839
Yeah. a coffee. black.

119
00:08:28.051 --> 00:08:30.417
I'm going back down to
headquarters after this.

120
00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.451
Okay. all right.

121
00:08:40.096 --> 00:08:41.063
Right. bye.

122
00:08:41.264 --> 00:08:43.323
How long do you think
this has been like this?

123
00:08:43.533 --> 00:08:45.364
I don't know. but we need to find out.

124
00:08:45.568 --> 00:08:47.399
The doctor's records say
the last time...

125
00:08:47.604 --> 00:08:50.471
...somebody got dropped off here
was five weeks ago.

126
00:08:51.074 --> 00:08:53.941
I mean. there's not even
a temporary office or anything.

127
00:08:54.611 --> 00:08:56.602
- How you doing?
- How you doing?

128
00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:16.126
Son of a bitch.

129
00:09:21.604 --> 00:09:22.628
What's the matter?

130
00:09:22.839 --> 00:09:25.501
I just made our perp.
Eleven o'clock. blue overcoat.

131
00:09:28.178 --> 00:09:30.738
- You sure that's him?
- A hundred percent.

132
00:09:31.414 --> 00:09:33.245
- Where did he come from?
- Shit if I know.

133
00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:36.180
I'm at the counter and
I see him rolling past the window.

134
00:09:36.386 --> 00:09:37.751
- Wanna go for the collar?
- No.

135
00:09:37.954 --> 00:09:40.582
We tail him. find out where he sleeps.
then take him down.

136
00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.725
A. B. C. Keep the box tight.

137
00:11:01.771 --> 00:11:06.538
- <i>Five-oh-two-six. Designator?</i>
- Samuel Koppler.

138
00:11:08.344 --> 00:11:09.572
<i>Message:</i>

139
00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:13.147
<i>Your uncle</i>
<i>wishes to see you immediately.</i>

140
00:11:13.349 --> 00:11:14.748
<i>Response?</i>

141
00:11:14.951 --> 00:11:19.684
The Guggenheim. fifth floor
of the rotunda. 40 minutes.

142
00:12:05.335 --> 00:12:06.859
- Hi. how you doing?
- Hello.

143
00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:09.300
N.Y.P.D. I need to
speak to your security chief.

144
00:12:09.506 --> 00:12:10.905
Okay. one moment.

145
00:12:12.008 --> 00:12:13.566
Rick?

146
00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.543
How you doing? Detective Ornelas.
I need to be able to clear security.

147
00:12:17.747 --> 00:12:19.180
- Okay.
- Thanks.

148
00:12:24.387 --> 00:12:26.048
We're clear.

149
00:12:57.554 --> 00:12:59.886
Directly behind me.

150
00:13:07.697 --> 00:13:09.528
There you go. Thank you.

151
00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.577
Who's the old scag
sitting next to him?

152
00:14:02.785 --> 00:14:05.982
I don't know. but I saw him at the
bank's headquarters in Luxembourg.

153
00:14:06.623 --> 00:14:09.285
You don't look well today.

154
00:14:09.726 --> 00:14:12.194
We all begin better than we end.

155
00:14:12.996 --> 00:14:15.328
What would you prefer your ending
to be like?

156
00:14:15.531 --> 00:14:20.468
Oh. more purposeful.
and certainly more climactic.

157
00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.562
A finale.

158
00:14:23.206 --> 00:14:24.798
A finale.

159
00:14:25.008 --> 00:14:28.535
Circumstances can always
be arranged.

160
00:14:29.545 --> 00:14:31.410
As much as the thought
appeals to me...

161
00:14:31.614 --> 00:14:35.277
...l'm afraid your consideration
is needed elsewhere.

162
00:14:36.152 --> 00:14:38.677
- What is this?
- Salinger.

163
00:14:39.255 --> 00:14:42.088
The method and manner
is entirely up to you.

164
00:14:42.291 --> 00:14:47.490
Your principle would simply like him
to vanish without a trace.

165
00:14:49.766 --> 00:14:53.065
- Any other provisions?
- Yes.

166
00:14:53.269 --> 00:14:54.566
No mistakes.

167
00:14:57.907 --> 00:14:59.704
I'll follow.

168
00:15:04.914 --> 00:15:08.213
- Where's Iggy going?
- Following a new lead.

169
00:15:37.013 --> 00:15:38.378
Shit.

170
00:15:38.581 --> 00:15:39.946
We gotta go.

171
00:15:41.584 --> 00:15:44.678
N.Y.P.D. Lock your hands
behind your head.

172
00:15:48.725 --> 00:15:49.851
Do it now.

173
00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:52.189
They'll never let you bring me in.

174
00:15:52.395 --> 00:15:54.454
Do it. or I'll take you down.

175
00:15:57.667 --> 00:15:58.929
- Cuffs.
- On the belt.

176
00:16:09.445 --> 00:16:10.810
There's a guy right up there.

177
00:16:38.541 --> 00:16:40.634
- Where'd he...?
- Up there! Up there!

178
00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.309
Get down!

179
00:16:59.128 --> 00:17:00.993
- God! Oh. my God!
- It's okay.

180
00:17:03.766 --> 00:17:04.755
Down there.

181
00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.441
Shit.

182
00:17:36.699 --> 00:17:37.688
Drop the gun.

183
00:17:39.001 --> 00:17:42.732
- If I drop the gun. we'll both die.
- I said. drop the gun!

184
00:17:42.939 --> 00:17:46.898
They're here for me but they'll kill
you too. Now help me get this off.

185
00:17:48.444 --> 00:17:49.638
I can't breathe.

186
00:18:12.602 --> 00:18:14.331
Stairs.

187
00:18:26.382 --> 00:18:28.282
- Fuck.
- You okay?

188
00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:32.887
The ramp is the only way out.

189
00:20:48.157 --> 00:20:49.784
Hey.

190
00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.020
Don't you fucking dare.

191
00:21:47.083 --> 00:21:49.278
<i>I'm calling from the dark side.</i>

192
00:21:49.485 --> 00:21:53.148
- Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
- <i>I'm calling from the...</i>

193
00:22:30.993 --> 00:22:32.290
Get back.

194
00:22:52.715 --> 00:22:54.376
I told you.

195
00:22:56.418 --> 00:22:58.784
What? You told me what?

196
00:23:00.322 --> 00:23:03.223
They'd never let you bring me in.

197
00:23:29.385 --> 00:23:30.374
Fuck. fuck.

198
00:23:40.496 --> 00:23:42.760
<i>Move away from the building.</i>

199
00:23:42.965 --> 00:23:46.833
<i>Can everybody please</i>
<i>move away from the building?</i>

200
00:24:05.421 --> 00:24:07.389
They know you're coming.
We gotta hurry.

201
00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:10.923
- Where'd they find him?
- Sitting on a bench near the reservoir.

202
00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.688
- Has he said anything yet?
- Nothing. He's pretty shaken up.

203
00:24:14.897 --> 00:24:18.697
- Who else knows he's here?
- Everyone. Nothing I could do.

204
00:24:18.901 --> 00:24:21.301
Heavies from the Bureau
and Justice are on their way.

205
00:24:21.503 --> 00:24:23.198
- <i>with an unidentified third man.</i>

206
00:24:23.405 --> 00:24:26.135
- How long do I have?
- Five. 10 minutes. max.

207
00:24:26.342 --> 00:24:28.867
- <i>wanted for questioning</i>
<i>in an ongoing investigation.</i>

208
00:24:29.178 --> 00:24:34.480
<i>Now. a Guggenheim employee tells me</i>
<i>that while they were in the museum...</i>

209
00:25:10.686 --> 00:25:12.881
This isn't over.

210
00:25:30.973 --> 00:25:32.600
Are you sure about this?

211
00:25:38.514 --> 00:25:39.503
Just read it.

212
00:25:54.963 --> 00:25:56.954
- They recognize you?
- Don't think so.

213
00:26:01.437 --> 00:26:03.405
Back it up!

214
00:26:44.913 --> 00:26:47.040
- <i>... screens came crashing down.</i>
- How you doing?

215
00:26:47.249 --> 00:26:50.582
- <i>There was glass everywhere.</i>
- As compared to what?

216
00:26:50.786 --> 00:26:52.617
<i>And just on the ground.</i>

217
00:26:52.821 --> 00:26:55.551
<i>When you heard all of this</i>
<i>commotion. did you think...?</i>

218
00:26:55.791 --> 00:26:57.725
Anything you need. Ellie.
just let me know.

219
00:26:57.926 --> 00:26:59.951
- Thanks.
- <i>I just heard gunshots.</i>

220
00:27:00.162 --> 00:27:02.289
<i>And people were hit</i>
<i>and screaming...</i>

221
00:27:02.498 --> 00:27:04.728
<i>... and people just started running</i>
<i>out the door...</i>

222
00:27:04.933 --> 00:27:06.662
<i>... and I didn't know</i>
<i>what was going on.</i>

223
00:27:06.869 --> 00:27:07.858
You okay?

224
00:27:08.637 --> 00:27:10.161
Yeah.

225
00:27:12.040 --> 00:27:14.133
You flip this guy.

226
00:27:14.610 --> 00:27:17.545
You make sure my partner
wasn't killed for nothing.

227
00:27:17.746 --> 00:27:21.477
<i>I know that... I think random people</i>
<i>were going down and...</i>

228
00:27:21.683 --> 00:27:26.211
<i>I mean. there was police running up</i>
<i>as other people were going down.</i>

229
00:27:38.734 --> 00:27:40.258
You ready for this?

230
00:28:16.939 --> 00:28:19.430
Good evening. Colonel Wexler.

231
00:28:21.243 --> 00:28:23.871
I'm Agent Louis Salinger.

232
00:28:24.680 --> 00:28:26.841
I know who you are.

233
00:28:28.717 --> 00:28:30.810
Of course you do.

234
00:28:32.855 --> 00:28:35.187
I was at the Guggenheim
this afternoon.

235
00:28:37.426 --> 00:28:39.018
<i>The assassin you met with...</i>

236
00:28:40.696 --> 00:28:42.789
<i>... I know you were his handler.</i>

237
00:28:42.998 --> 00:28:46.161
I know you arranged for him
to be killed at the behest of the bank...

238
00:28:46.368 --> 00:28:48.563
...because I was obviously
getting too close.

239
00:28:51.874 --> 00:28:54.570
But if a hit team at the Guggenheim
is what happens...

240
00:28:54.776 --> 00:28:57.574
...because I was
getting too close to him...

241
00:29:00.148 --> 00:29:03.845
...what do you think the bank'll do
when it realizes how close I am to you?

242
00:29:04.052 --> 00:29:08.614
Death comes for us all.
Agent Salinger.

243
00:29:09.358 --> 00:29:11.417
But based on everything
I've read about you...

244
00:29:11.627 --> 00:29:13.322
...you seem like the kind of man...

245
00:29:13.529 --> 00:29:16.430
...who aspired to die
for something more than this.

246
00:29:18.233 --> 00:29:22.727
Well. this is the difference
between truth and fiction.

247
00:29:24.072 --> 00:29:26.336
Fiction has to make sense.

248
00:29:29.111 --> 00:29:31.011
I'm confused. colonel.

249
00:29:34.182 --> 00:29:36.377
Why would a tried
and true communist...

250
00:29:37.486 --> 00:29:39.852
...a hardliner that spent 30 years
in the Stasi...

251
00:29:40.055 --> 00:29:42.216
...fighting against the evils
of capitalism...

252
00:29:42.925 --> 00:29:46.088
Why would this man waste his
final days working for an institution...

253
00:29:46.295 --> 00:29:49.458
...that was the very embodiment
of everything he once despised?

254
00:29:52.501 --> 00:29:55.368
You dedicated your life
to the communist ideal.

255
00:29:57.806 --> 00:30:01.173
You sacrificed everything
for the good of the party.

256
00:30:02.711 --> 00:30:04.042
For what?

257
00:30:07.783 --> 00:30:10.411
You lost your wife to betrayal...

258
00:30:11.053 --> 00:30:13.544
...your daughter to suicide...

259
00:30:14.923 --> 00:30:18.154
...and when the Wall fell.
your whole life fell apart with it.

260
00:30:18.460 --> 00:30:20.724
You know nothing about me.

261
00:30:21.296 --> 00:30:24.163
I was lost long before the Wall fell.

262
00:30:25.400 --> 00:30:30.099
I was once destined to become
a man much like yourself.

263
00:30:30.539 --> 00:30:32.336
True-hearted...

264
00:30:32.674 --> 00:30:34.642
...determined...

265
00:30:34.843 --> 00:30:36.811
...full of purpose.

266
00:30:37.813 --> 00:30:39.713
But...

267
00:30:40.182 --> 00:30:42.912
...character is easier kept
than recovered.

268
00:30:44.152 --> 00:30:48.020
We cannot control
the things life does to us.

269
00:30:48.690 --> 00:30:52.626
They are done before you know it.
and once they are done...

270
00:30:54.029 --> 00:30:56.190
...they make you do other things...

271
00:30:56.798 --> 00:30:59.995
...until at last.
everything comes between you...

272
00:31:01.036 --> 00:31:03.527
...and the man you wanted to be.

273
00:31:05.474 --> 00:31:06.941
No.

274
00:31:08.877 --> 00:31:12.040
We all have choices in life.
You made yours.

275
00:31:19.454 --> 00:31:21.251
Sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

276
00:31:21.456 --> 00:31:23.287
...on the road he took to avoid it.

277
00:31:26.528 --> 00:31:29.258
Skarssen and that bank need to
answer for what they've done.

278
00:31:29.464 --> 00:31:31.432
They have to be brought to justice.

279
00:31:31.633 --> 00:31:33.567
You can help me do that.

280
00:31:33.902 --> 00:31:35.699
Justice...

281
00:31:36.538 --> 00:31:38.472
...is not possible.

282
00:31:39.141 --> 00:31:40.608
Why not?

283
00:31:41.076 --> 00:31:43.567
Because. Agent Salinger...

284
00:31:43.779 --> 00:31:47.715
...your idea of justice is an illusion.

285
00:31:48.483 --> 00:31:51.008
<i>Understand the very system</i>
<i>that you serve and protect...</i>

286
00:31:51.219 --> 00:31:54.746
<i>... will never allow anything to happen</i>
<i>to Skarssen or the bank.</i>

287
00:31:55.357 --> 00:31:56.915
On the contrary.

288
00:31:57.325 --> 00:32:01.386
The system guarantees
the IBBC's safety...

289
00:32:01.830 --> 00:32:05.061
...because everyone is involved.

290
00:32:05.867 --> 00:32:07.801
What do you mean. "everyone"?

291
00:32:10.639 --> 00:32:12.072
Hezbollah.

292
00:32:12.607 --> 00:32:14.541
CIA.

293
00:32:15.043 --> 00:32:16.738
The Columbian drug cartels.

294
00:32:17.145 --> 00:32:19.306
Russian organized crime.

295
00:32:19.514 --> 00:32:22.950
Governments of Iran. Germany.
China. your government.

296
00:32:23.185 --> 00:32:26.245
Every multinational corporation.
every one.

297
00:32:26.688 --> 00:32:30.988
They all need banks like the IBBC...

298
00:32:31.193 --> 00:32:36.062
...so that they can operate
within the black and gray latitudes.

299
00:32:36.465 --> 00:32:38.490
And this is why
your investigative efforts...

300
00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:42.261
...have either been ignored
or undermined...

301
00:32:42.471 --> 00:32:45.599
...and why you and I
will be quietly disposed of...

302
00:32:46.608 --> 00:32:51.636
...before any case against the bank
ever reaches a court of law.

303
00:32:57.786 --> 00:32:59.811
<i>So. what are we all</i>
<i>supposed to do?</i>

304
00:33:03.158 --> 00:33:05.422
We just supposed to give up...

305
00:33:05.727 --> 00:33:08.491
...and accept that
this is the way of the world?

306
00:33:12.968 --> 00:33:14.731
I'm not gonna do that.

307
00:33:16.171 --> 00:33:19.334
I still believe... I know...

308
00:33:19.541 --> 00:33:22.942
...that there has to be a way
to bring down this bank...

309
00:33:23.578 --> 00:33:25.944
...and you are gonna help me.

310
00:33:33.088 --> 00:33:35.249
You understand...

311
00:33:36.625 --> 00:33:40.356
...if you really want to
stop the IBBC...

312
00:33:41.096 --> 00:33:46.261
...you won't be able to do it within the
boundaries of your system of justice.

313
00:33:46.902 --> 00:33:49.268
You will have to go outside.

314
00:33:50.038 --> 00:33:51.596
Once you do...

315
00:33:53.275 --> 00:33:56.767
...there will always be
collateral damage.

316
00:34:01.516 --> 00:34:03.245
<i>Yes.</i>

317
00:34:04.319 --> 00:34:08.722
<i>Should you sacrifice your own ideals</i>
<i>for the greater good?</i>

318
00:34:09.891 --> 00:34:13.691
That's a difficult choice.
one I understand all too well...

319
00:34:14.629 --> 00:34:16.859
...but as you so eloquently put it...

320
00:34:17.299 --> 00:34:20.632
...sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

321
00:34:20.836 --> 00:34:24.237
...on the road he took to avoid it.

322
00:34:36.151 --> 00:34:37.243
What?

323
00:34:37.452 --> 00:34:38.680
What are you doing?

324
00:34:39.321 --> 00:34:41.221
I think it's time for you to leave.

325
00:34:41.890 --> 00:34:46.589
- Leave? What are you talking about?
- You know what I'm talking about.

326
00:34:50.131 --> 00:34:51.962
No way. Lou.

327
00:34:52.167 --> 00:34:55.034
No fucking way.
You've already got him turned.

328
00:34:55.237 --> 00:34:58.638
Now go back in there
and get him to come in on his own.

329
00:34:59.174 --> 00:35:02.200
We can use everything.
We'll blow this whole thing wide open.

330
00:35:02.410 --> 00:35:04.708
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

331
00:35:04.913 --> 00:35:06.904
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

332
00:35:07.115 --> 00:35:10.676
- I can protect him. Lou.
- No. you can't. They'll get to him.

333
00:35:10.886 --> 00:35:12.444
If they can't. they'll get to you.

334
00:35:12.654 --> 00:35:15.054
If they can't get to you.
they'll get to your family.

335
00:35:27.769 --> 00:35:29.930
I can't just walk away from this.

336
00:35:31.239 --> 00:35:34.037
You're walking away
so I don't have to.

337
00:35:42.984 --> 00:35:44.417
How can you trust him?

338
00:35:44.886 --> 00:35:48.014
That relic in there
is looking for redemption.

339
00:35:48.223 --> 00:35:50.248
I'm the only one
who can give it to him.

340
00:35:51.326 --> 00:35:54.159
Then who gives it to you
when this is all over?

341
00:35:55.864 --> 00:35:57.923
You need to cut me loose.

342
00:36:00.535 --> 00:36:03.265
Tell them I escaped from custody.
whatever you have to.

343
00:36:03.471 --> 00:36:05.462
Just use my history.
They'll believe you.

344
00:36:05.674 --> 00:36:07.938
- I don't know.
- Ella. listen to me.

345
00:36:09.811 --> 00:36:11.176
Sometimes the hardest thing...

346
00:36:11.379 --> 00:36:14.371
...is to know which bridge to cross
and which to burn.

347
00:36:18.787 --> 00:36:20.982
I'm the one you burn.

348
00:37:20.582 --> 00:37:22.641
We've been waiting here
for an hour.

349
00:37:22.851 --> 00:37:26.651
I'm sorry. Martin. but none of us
have been able to reach them.

350
00:37:27.222 --> 00:37:31.716
Unfortunately. Mario and Enzo Calvini
are not known for their punctuality.

351
00:37:31.926 --> 00:37:33.757
They do realize this is the closing?

352
00:37:56.551 --> 00:37:57.882
Mr. White...

353
00:37:58.086 --> 00:38:01.544
...l've been instructed to escort you
and your associates from the building.

354
00:38:01.756 --> 00:38:03.815
Please gather your materials
and come with me.

355
00:38:04.025 --> 00:38:07.552
- Instructed by whom?
- Please. if you could just comply.

356
00:38:29.784 --> 00:38:32.412
Our father
never trusted these people.

357
00:38:34.055 --> 00:38:37.183
Thank you for telling us the truth.

358
00:38:40.795 --> 00:38:42.626
Had you not come forward...

359
00:38:42.831 --> 00:38:45.231
...we would have made
a terrible mistake today.

360
00:38:45.433 --> 00:38:48.095
I'm just glad I could be of service.

361
00:38:54.442 --> 00:38:58.105
I don't know. Jonas. I was told nothing.
I was simply thrown out.

362
00:38:58.580 --> 00:39:00.343
<i>They know.</i>

363
00:39:06.821 --> 00:39:11.121
Look. I can't discuss this right now.
I'll call you when I'm in the air.

364
00:39:36.718 --> 00:39:39.209
<i>Welcome to World News.</i>
<i>I'm Tristana Moore.</i>

365
00:39:39.420 --> 00:39:42.821
<i>We're live today in the</i>
<i>Democratic Republic of Niberia.</i>

366
00:39:43.024 --> 00:39:46.050
<i>As we go on air. we're getting reports</i>
<i>that thousands of troops...</i>

367
00:39:46.261 --> 00:39:49.890
<i>... loyal to General Charles Motomba's</i>
<i>Revolutionary Freedom Front...</i>

368
00:39:50.098 --> 00:39:52.658
<i>... are moving towards</i>
<i>the capital of Dénué.</i>

369
00:39:52.867 --> 00:39:55.802
<i>According to eyewitnesses.</i>
<i>several explosions have been heard...</i>

370
00:39:56.004 --> 00:39:59.997
<i>... and there've been heavy outbreaks</i>
<i>of gunfire in many parts of the city.</i>

371
00:40:00.208 --> 00:40:02.870
<i>The people of Niberia</i>
<i>have suffered greatly.</i>

372
00:40:03.077 --> 00:40:06.513
<i>It is time to begin a new chapter</i>
<i>in our country's history.</i>

373
00:40:06.714 --> 00:40:09.581
<i>We will not stop</i>
<i>until national liberation...</i>

374
00:40:09.784 --> 00:40:12.252
<i>... and the restoration of nationhood...</i>

375
00:40:17.058 --> 00:40:18.082
News about Martin?

376
00:40:19.060 --> 00:40:21.551
He didn't show up at his hotel
or at the airport.

377
00:40:21.763 --> 00:40:26.325
The Italian police have been unable
to locate his car or driver.

378
00:40:26.534 --> 00:40:30.197
I think Enzo and Mario Calvini
are sending us a message.

379
00:40:30.405 --> 00:40:32.771
How could they possibly
have found out?

380
00:40:36.544 --> 00:40:39.069
This is precisely
what we pay you to know.

381
00:40:39.280 --> 00:40:40.770
We're out of time and options.

382
00:40:41.182 --> 00:40:45.084
- We must make the deal with Sunay.
- How can we trust this man?

383
00:40:45.286 --> 00:40:48.414
The Israeli government
is his biggest customer.

384
00:40:48.623 --> 00:40:49.715
Why would he agree...

385
00:40:49.924 --> 00:40:53.485
...to help us provide missiles
to the Iranians and the Syrians...

386
00:40:53.695 --> 00:40:56.425
...that have a first-strike capability
against the Israelis?

387
00:40:56.631 --> 00:40:59.099
I know Sunay.
I believe he has every intention...

388
00:40:59.300 --> 00:41:01.131
...of selling you
the guidance systems...

389
00:41:01.569 --> 00:41:03.730
...because he's already provided
the Israelis...

390
00:41:03.938 --> 00:41:06.771
...with the countermeasures
to defeat them.

391
00:41:08.676 --> 00:41:11.474
Would the Turk really play
such a dangerous game?

392
00:41:12.981 --> 00:41:14.608
We are.

393
00:41:15.750 --> 00:41:18.014
The only way we can make this work...

394
00:41:18.219 --> 00:41:19.208
...is to guarantee...

395
00:41:19.420 --> 00:41:22.150
...that Sunay keeps this information
in complete confidence.

396
00:41:22.357 --> 00:41:26.293
If our buyers find out the missiles are
worthless. they'll pull all their orders...

397
00:41:26.494 --> 00:41:28.826
...and this bank will be left insolvent.

398
00:41:29.330 --> 00:41:31.264
Have him here
by tomorrow afternoon.

399
00:41:31.466 --> 00:41:34.697
Tomorrow he's going to
a funeral service for his cousin.

400
00:41:34.902 --> 00:41:36.767
He'll be unavailable till Monday.

401
00:41:37.405 --> 00:41:40.499
Unless of course.
you'd be willing to attend.

402
00:41:41.976 --> 00:41:43.773
Make the call.

403
00:41:46.247 --> 00:41:48.545
Get me Ahmet Sunay.

404
00:41:55.356 --> 00:41:57.324
It's tomorrow.

405
00:42:38.533 --> 00:42:41.093
It's right there.
Do you want to be escorted?

406
00:42:41.302 --> 00:42:42.735
We'll be fine. thank you.

407
00:42:48.710 --> 00:42:50.143
The Sunay funeral. please.

408
00:42:50.345 --> 00:42:52.643
It will be over soon.
You may wait here.

409
00:42:52.847 --> 00:42:56.840
- Is there a bathroom I could use?
- Just over there.

410
00:42:57.051 --> 00:42:59.986
- I won't be a moment.
- Right.

411
00:43:06.494 --> 00:43:08.655
- The signal?
- Good.

412
00:43:08.863 --> 00:43:10.228
<i>The Sunay funeral. please.</i>

413
00:43:10.865 --> 00:43:14.392
- Where'd you put the spike?
- Inside the lapel of his jacket.

414
00:43:15.603 --> 00:43:16.661
The lawyer?

415
00:43:17.872 --> 00:43:19.430
White?

416
00:43:19.674 --> 00:43:20.698
He's gone.

417
00:43:22.443 --> 00:43:26.311
I told you. there will always
be collateral damage...

418
00:43:26.514 --> 00:43:28.778
...when you take matters
into your own hands.

419
00:43:31.219 --> 00:43:32.243
Your plan is working.

420
00:43:33.187 --> 00:43:35.417
It has left Skarssen
with only one option.

421
00:43:35.623 --> 00:43:39.320
Record the conversation
and you'll gain your end.

422
00:43:41.496 --> 00:43:45.023
Sure they'll talk about Sunay's deal
with Israel and the countermeasures?

423
00:43:45.233 --> 00:43:46.564
It is the key issue.

424
00:43:46.768 --> 00:43:48.702
Once you let the Iranians
and Syrians...

425
00:43:48.903 --> 00:43:53.465
...hear that the missiles are completely
useless against the Israelis...

426
00:43:53.975 --> 00:43:59.811
...they will cancel their orders
and the IBBC will collapse.

427
00:44:08.489 --> 00:44:10.582
- Wilhelm.
- Ahmet.

428
00:44:11.092 --> 00:44:12.389
It's been a long time.

429
00:44:12.760 --> 00:44:13.749
<i>Yes.</i>

430
00:44:13.961 --> 00:44:15.826
<i>My sympathies for the loss</i>
<i>of your cousin.</i>

431
00:44:16.030 --> 00:44:17.258
Thank you.

432
00:44:17.465 --> 00:44:20.059
Jonas Skarssen. Ahmet Sunay.

433
00:44:20.268 --> 00:44:24.432
If you'd simply come to me in the
beginning. it would have been better.

434
00:44:27.275 --> 00:44:29.072
<i>Midday prayers will begin soon.</i>

435
00:44:29.277 --> 00:44:31.802
Should take a short time
to settle on the broad strokes.

436
00:44:32.013 --> 00:44:33.878
<i>The rest can be sorted out</i>
<i>at your leisure.</i>

437
00:44:34.081 --> 00:44:35.070
<i>We have 10 minutes.</i>

438
00:44:47.195 --> 00:44:50.528
Wilhelm. would you mind
if I spoke to Mr. Sunay alone?

439
00:44:55.770 --> 00:44:59.399
I believe I understand
the particulars of your situation.

440
00:44:59.607 --> 00:45:02.440
<i>Perhaps we should discuss this</i>
<i>in a more private place.</i>

441
00:45:02.643 --> 00:45:04.304
<i>Yes. of course.</i>

442
00:45:04.712 --> 00:45:07.340
<i>Allow me to show you something</i>
<i>very special.</i>

443
00:45:07.548 --> 00:45:11.314
<i>Something that very few outsiders</i>
<i>know exists.</i>

444
00:45:12.820 --> 00:45:17.519
<i>It's my understanding that the product</i>
<i>you purchased are the XW-41 s.</i>

445
00:45:17.992 --> 00:45:19.016
After you.

446
00:45:19.227 --> 00:45:21.559
<i>Yes. Forty-two hundred units.</i>

447
00:45:23.831 --> 00:45:26.664
What kind of guidance
are they currently equipped...?

448
00:45:31.906 --> 00:45:34.898
<i>They all need to be upgraded</i>
<i>with VOLCON systems.</i>

449
00:45:35.710 --> 00:45:37.371
<i>Launch platforms?</i>

450
00:45:37.578 --> 00:45:40.138
<i>Ground-based vehicles</i>
<i>and fixed-wing aircraft.</i>

451
00:45:50.591 --> 00:45:53.151
So you understand
I have a terminal deadline.

452
00:45:53.361 --> 00:45:55.158
First of February. yes.

453
00:45:55.363 --> 00:45:57.263
- <i>Can you meet it?</i>
- <i>To be sure.</i>

454
00:45:57.465 --> 00:46:01.060
<i>But you must arrange for the</i>
<i>end-user certificates. transport...</i>

455
00:46:01.269 --> 00:46:02.793
<i>We'll arrange for it all.</i>

456
00:46:03.004 --> 00:46:04.437
<i>Where would the work be done?</i>

457
00:46:04.639 --> 00:46:07.506
<i>Cyprus. I've a facility there.</i>

458
00:46:08.943 --> 00:46:12.504
<i>We would start retrofitting the worms</i>
<i>within a day of their arrival.</i>

459
00:46:12.713 --> 00:46:15.773
<i>So if you deliver them to me</i>
<i>within the next two weeks...</i>

460
00:46:15.983 --> 00:46:17.917
<i>... we'll meet your deadline.</i>

461
00:46:30.498 --> 00:46:33.763
I'm concerned that we limit any and all
knowledge of your involvement.

462
00:46:34.468 --> 00:46:37.869
<i>If we structure my involvement</i>
<i>through a thick veil of shells...</i>

463
00:46:39.073 --> 00:46:41.041
<i>... I don't foresee any complications.</i>

464
00:46:42.476 --> 00:46:45.206
- Sorry?
- You. Come here now.

465
00:46:45.413 --> 00:46:48.439
<i>Usually we would involve</i>
<i>our import partners from Russia.</i>

466
00:46:48.883 --> 00:46:50.316
What? I'm just a tourist.

467
00:46:50.518 --> 00:46:53.112
- Now. you must leave.
- Could you get that light out of...?

468
00:46:53.321 --> 00:46:55.949
Get your fucking...

469
00:46:58.125 --> 00:47:01.617
So. shall we discuss numbers?

470
00:47:02.063 --> 00:47:03.758
There is a more salient deal point...

471
00:47:03.965 --> 00:47:06.763
...that needs to be resolved
before we can do that.

472
00:47:06.968 --> 00:47:08.765
<i>And what point is that?</i>

473
00:47:09.770 --> 00:47:12.000
<i>The point of fidelity.</i>

474
00:47:19.180 --> 00:47:21.205
I know you provided
the Israeli government...

475
00:47:21.415 --> 00:47:24.350
...with the countermeasures
to this guidance system.

476
00:47:32.460 --> 00:47:34.519
Last year alone...

477
00:47:34.729 --> 00:47:38.290
...I did more than 300 million
in business with the Israelis.

478
00:47:42.003 --> 00:47:44.301
I would never put that at risk.

479
00:47:44.505 --> 00:47:48.703
How can I trust you not to divulge
this information to anyone else?

480
00:47:49.677 --> 00:47:52.202
It's mutual interest. not trust...

481
00:47:52.647 --> 00:47:55.275
...that will be the bond
of our relationship.

482
00:47:59.053 --> 00:48:01.886
Your compensation will be held
in an escrow account.

483
00:48:03.124 --> 00:48:05.319
- <i>released until our clients pay</i>
<i>in full.</i>

484
00:48:06.027 --> 00:48:07.358
And those are the terms.

485
00:48:10.131 --> 00:48:11.758
<i>The payout structure...</i>

486
00:48:14.168 --> 00:48:16.466
<i>The transfers will be begun</i>
<i>by tomorrow morning.</i>

487
00:48:16.671 --> 00:48:20.163
<i>Ehames will contact you with</i>
<i>the number for the escrow account.</i>

488
00:48:25.479 --> 00:48:28.471
So ends the bloody business
of the day.

489
00:48:41.328 --> 00:48:43.694
We're closed. I need you and Ehames
here tomorrow...

490
00:48:43.898 --> 00:48:46.458
...to work out all the details
with Sunay's people.

491
00:48:46.867 --> 00:48:49.597
Yes. We're on our way home.

492
00:48:57.445 --> 00:48:58.434
Wilhelm?

493
00:49:01.449 --> 00:49:02.848
Wake up.

494
00:52:03.898 --> 00:52:04.887
Who are you?

495
00:52:07.134 --> 00:52:08.897
I'm Louis Salinger.

496
00:52:18.879 --> 00:52:21.575
You don't have the authority
to arrest me.

497
00:52:23.851 --> 00:52:26.547
Who said anything
about arresting you?

498
00:52:30.891 --> 00:52:34.622
- What do you want?
- I want some fucking justice.

499
00:52:34.828 --> 00:52:38.525
Wait. wait. Wait.
Executing me won't change anything.

500
00:52:38.732 --> 00:52:41.223
There will be 100 other bankers
to take my place.

501
00:52:41.435 --> 00:52:44.427
Everything will continue.

502
00:52:44.638 --> 00:52:50.577
The only thing you'll succeed in doing
is to satisfy your own blood lust.

503
00:52:55.516 --> 00:52:56.949
And you know it.

504
00:53:51.605 --> 00:53:54.233
With compliments of Enzo
and Mario Calvini.

505
00:54:09.390 --> 00:54:10.857
Thank you.

